course: dictionary
lesson: 7500
title: Posture: how you hold yourself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Posture is the way you hold your body when you stand, sit or walk. «Using a phone or controller for a long time can strain hands, wrists and neck; good posture and breaks help.» So posture is about how your body sits or stands, and it matters for comfort.
explain: Good posture means a straight back, relaxed shoulders and feet flat on the floor. «Slumping squashes the chest and belly, so there is less air» shows that bad posture can make breathing harder. Sitting up straight is one way to improve your posture.
explain: Posture can also mean the attitude someone shows towards something. In a story, a writer may describe a character's posture to show how they feel. «His slumped posture showed he was sad» tells you about his feelings, not just his body. Upright posture can show confidence.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. «There is no single perfect posture; changing position often and getting up to move about every half hour is good for the body.» This tells you posture is not one fixed pose: moving and changing position matters too.
fact: Posture is the way you hold your body when you stand, sit or walk.
fact: Good posture: a straight back, shoulders relaxed, feet flat.
fact: Bad posture: slouching or slumping, often over a screen or a controller.
fact: «Posture» can also mean the attitude someone shows, and writers use it to show feelings.
fact: Changing position often and getting up to move every half hour is good for the body.
exercise: «Her posture was straight and proud as she walked onto the stage.» What does posture mean here? | The name of the stage | *The way she held her body | A kind of costume | A loud noise
exercise: Mum says, «Sit up straight, and mind your posture.» What should you do? | *Sit with your back straight and your shoulders relaxed | Hunch over your phone with your head down | Lie flat on the sofa | Slide right down into the chair
exercise: «His slumped posture showed he was sad.» Find and copy one word that tells you how he was feeling. | window | *slumped | boy | sat
test: «Good posture can help your back feel better, especially if you sit for a long time.» Which part of the body does good posture help? | *Your back | Your shoes | Your phone | Your hair
test: Which one is an example of good posture? | Leaning on the desk with your chin in your hands | *Back straight, shoulders relaxed, feet flat | Slumped over a screen with a curved back | Curled up on the floor
exam: Ella thinks posture only means how you stand. What does posture really mean? | A kind of shoe you wear for exercise | A type of healthy food | A loud noise made by a chair | *The way you hold your body when you stand, sit or walk
